# The M9 Hyper-V check's burst-15 run (tools/hyperv/README.md, "At the M9
# check"; docs/design.md, "Transmit and receive"): m8-release.scenario with
# uart.burst=15 on the command line, the burst setup chooses with working
# FIFOs, as the M8 check found Hyper-V's: the control for
# m9-burst1.scenario, whose lines differ from these by a digit, and the
# same writes as the M8 re-run's. Both M8 runs lost a few bytes of one of
# root's lines during the flood of its summary with burst 15. Lines whole
# with burst 1 but cut with 15 mean Hyper-V's FIFO takes fewer bytes after
# it reports THRE than uart writes; cut either way points at the named
# pipe. The scenario cannot see a cut line it does not expect, so the
# session reads each of root's lines in the log: run it twice. Root's line
# "root: uart.burst=15: uart's burst capped at 15" comes right after its
# cmdline line, but is not expected, so that bytes lost there leave the
# run going. The release kernel prints nothing; root issues no exit port,
# since this is not QEMU, and halts after TEST PASS; the script turns the
# VM off. The typed line is 14 bytes, whose last 6 only the character
# timeout delivers.
cmdline: test=release uart.burst=15
kernel: release
exit: success
expect: loader: microL4 loader
expect: entering kernel
next: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=release uart.burst=15"
expect: root: image frames: slots
expect: root: empty: slots
expect: release: watch (priority 255), uart (priority 200) with the COM1 IOPort and IRQ 4, console (priority 150); exit port none: not QEMU
expect: release: a probe thread's DebugPutChar, DebugHalt, DebugDumpScheduler and reserved numbers 19 and 31 each raised UnknownSyscall with the number in MR18
expect: release: type a line
send: release input\r
expect: release: read "release input"
expect: release: uart:
expect: , 14 bytes received,
expect: , 0 overruns, 0 line errors,
expect: , burst 15, # working FIFOs, under the cap
expect: TEST PASS
forbid: microL4 kernel
forbid: bootinfo:
forbid: DEBUG HALT
forbid: KERNEL PANIC
forbid: , 0 THRE bursts
forbid: ignored: not a number
